<div id="settingsSlots" hidden><select id="langSelect" class="btn small" aria-label="Language" title="Language" data-no-i18n></select><select class="btn small a2navsel" aria-label="Menu position" title="Menu position"><option value="top">Menu: Top</option><option value="left">Menu: Left</option><option value="right">Menu: Right</option></select>
<section class="card only-full" id="controls">
  <div class="row">
    <span class="lbl g" id="regionLbl">Region</span>
    <div class="seg" id="regionSeg" role="group" aria-labelledby="regionLbl">
      <button data-region="TW">Taiwan (UTC+8)</button>
      <button data-region="KR">Korea (UTC+9)</button>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="row">
    <span class="lbl g" id="globalLbl">Global</span>
    <div class="seg" id="globalSeg" role="group" aria-labelledby="globalLbl">
      <button data-region="NAW">NA West</button>
      <button data-region="NAE">NA East</button>
      <button data-region="SA">South America</button>
      <button data-region="EU">Europe</button>
      <button data-region="JP">Japan</button>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="row">
    <label class="lbl" for="tzSelect">Show times in</label>
    <select id="tzSelect" aria-label="Display time zone"></select>
    <button class="btn small" id="tzReset" title="Use the time zone your device reports">Auto</button>
  </div>
  <div class="row">
    <span class="lbl g" id="factionLbl">Faction</span>
    <div class="seg" id="factionSeg" role="group" aria-labelledby="factionLbl"><button data-f="">Not Set</button><button data-f="elyos">Elyos</button><button data-f="asmo">Asmodian</button></div>
  </div>
  <div class="row">
    <label class="lbl" for="fbServerSel">Your server</label>
    <select id="fbServerSel" class="fb-in" aria-label="Server"></select>
    <input id="fbServer" class="fb-in hidden" placeholder="Server name" maxlength="24" aria-label="Server name">
  </div>
  <div class="row">
    <label class="lbl" for="mainClass">Main class (optional)</label>
    <select id="mainClass" class="fb-in" aria-label="Main class"><option value="">Select class</option></select>
    <button class="btn small" id="buildOptsBtn" hidden>Build options</button>
  </div>
  <div class="row"><span class="subtle">Pick your faction first: every Aion 2 server belongs to one, so the server list follows it. The server is used for shared field boss kills and party posts; choosing one also sets your region.</span></div>
</section>
</div>
<main id="main" tabindex="-1">

<section class="hero only-full" id="hero">
  <img class="hero-banner" src="/img/aion2timers-logo.png" alt="" width="797" height="495" fetchpriority="high">
  <h1 class="hero-welcome">Welcome to Aion 2 Timers</h1>
</section>
<template data-topic-content="spacetime-rift-timer"><h2 class="tp-title" id="tpTitle">Aion 2 Spacetime Rift Timer</h2><p>This is a live <strong>Aion 2 Spacetime Rift timer</strong>. The big countdown shows exactly when the next rift portal opens on your server, converted to your own time zone by your browser, so it stays correct through daylight-saving changes. While a rift is active it switches to the portal-close countdown, because the entry portal only stays open for about ten minutes.</p></template><template data-topic-content="world-boss-timer"><h2 class="tp-title" id="tpTitle">Aion 2 Field Boss Timers</h2><p>Every <strong>Aion 2 field boss</strong> (also called a world boss) on one page: respawn countdowns for your server, kept up to date by players and the AbyssLogs DPS Meter, and the scheduled Reshanta (Abyss) spawns counted down in your local time.</p>
<p>Field bosses have a preset spawn timer that starts the moment they are killed. Aion2Timers is partnered with <a href="https://abysslogs.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">AbyssLogs DPS Meter</a> to send data to Aion2Timers to provide realtime feed to this Field Boss Tracker. It will monitor and track Field Boss kills and respawns while you're out and about. You can also setup a Discord alert for when servers respawn from the <a href="/discord-alerts/">Discord alerts page</a>.</p></template><template data-topic-content="daily-reset"><h2 class="tp-title" id="tpTitle">Aion 2 Daily Reset and Weekly Reset Time</h2><p>The <strong>Aion 2 daily reset</strong> happens at <strong>05:00 server time</strong> and the <strong>weekly reset</strong> on <strong>Wednesday at 05:00 server time</strong>. The clocks above show the countdown to both in your local time, and the Checklist (in the menu) clears itself automatically when each reset passes.</p>
<h2>What resets daily</h2>
<ul><li>Mission quests (5 per day), Nightmare solo boss (2 per day), Expedition: Conquest (3 per day).</li><li>Transcendence charges (+1 per day, cap 14), Shugo Festival keys, Dimensional Invasion charges (+1 per day, cap 7).</li><li>Daily supply requests and the Black Cloud Merchant hourly stock cycle.</li></ul>
<h2>What resets weekly (Wednesday 05:00)</h2>
<ul><li>Command Missions (12), 4-player raids (3), the Ladra 10-player raid (2), Ascension Test (3), Expedition: Exploration (7), Odyle Energy Morph (7).</li><li>Daily dungeon entries: 7 free per week (up to 30 with tickets). They do not require daily logins, so you can clear all seven in one sitting before Wednesday.</li><li>Abyss weekly reward caps, Vakron Trial Subjugation Marks, Sanctuary and Snowfield of Sorrow boss clears, Shugo Festival keys (7 per week, 14 with membership).</li></ul>
<p>Server time is UTC+9 on Korea and UTC+8 on Taiwan. Global NA, SA, EU and Japan servers open October 5, 2026 and their reset clock has not been published yet; this page will be updated the moment it is.</p></template><template data-topic-content="release-countdown"><h2 class="tp-title" id="tpTitle">Aion 2 Release Date Countdown</h2><p>Counting down to the <strong>Aion 2 global release</strong>. NCSOFT launches Aion 2 in North America, South America, Europe and Japan on <strong>Monday, October 5, 2026 at 6:00 AM PDT (13:00 UTC)</strong> on Steam and the PURPLE launcher, free to play. Founder's Pack owners get five days of <strong>Advance Access from September 30 to October 4</strong>, with the <strong>pre-download open from September 28 at 6:00 AM PDT</strong>. The Launch Scale Test on September 17 and 18 has ended.</p>
<h2>Key dates</h2>
<ul><li><strong>Launch Scale Test (ended):</strong> September 17 and 18. Level cap 37, all progress wiped afterward, no Founder's Pack was needed.</li><li><strong>Pre-download:</strong> Monday, September 28 at 6:00 AM PDT (9:00 AM EDT, 15:00 CEST, 13:00 UTC) on Steam and PURPLE, announced on the official AION 2 channel. Install early so you can log in the moment Advance Access opens.</li><li><strong>Advance Access:</strong> September 30 to October 4 with any Founder's Pack ($24.99, $49.99 or $99.99). Opened at 7:00 AM PDT (14:00 UTC): NCSOFT pushed it back one hour from 6:00 AM in official notices on September 30.</li><li><strong>Global launch:</strong> Monday, October 5, 2026 at 6:00 AM PDT, which is 9:00 AM EDT, 15:00 CEST, 22:00 JST and 13:00 UTC, per the official Steam store page. Servers: North America, South America, Europe and Japan (Asia).</li></ul>
<p>The pre-download and the October 5 launch run to 13:00 UTC and Advance Access to 14:00 UTC, converted to your time zone. If NCSOFT changes any of these hours, the countdown will be updated the same day. Want a Discord message 30 minutes before each milestone? Use the <a href="/discord-alerts/">Discord alerts page</a> and tick launch milestones.</p>
<script src="/js/release.js?v=c284974bf3" defer></script></template><template data-topic-content="discord-alerts"><h2 class="tp-title" id="tpTitle">Aion 2 Discord Alerts</h2><p>Post <strong>Aion 2 alerts to your Discord server</strong> with nothing more than a webhook URL. Pick the events below, set how many minutes before each one you want the ping, paste the webhook, and our alert server does the rest. The preview shows the exact message first. Unlike a browser alert it keeps working when this page is closed, and you can add a live timer board: one message in your channel that keeps itself up to date. Prefer asking a bot? The Aion 2 Timers bot answers <code>!timer rift</code> in any channel.</p>
<h2>What you can be alerted about</h2>
<ul><li>Spacetime Rift openings (with the portal-close time in the message), Rift Domination, Abyss Rift Zone, Artifact Conquest and Abyss battlefield hours.</li><li>Reshanta world bosses: the post-Conquest bosses, Enraged Guardian Lord Nahma and the Watcher Kaira cycle.</li><li>Shugo Festival, Dimensional Invasion, Beritra Air Raid and the Black Cloud Merchant refresh (hourly, so enable with care).</li><li>Daily and weekly resets, and the global launch milestones.</li></ul>
<h2>How it works</h2>
<p>Messages use Discord's own timestamp format, so every member sees the time in their local zone. You can ping @here, @everyone or a specific role, and field boss respawn alerts can be narrowed to the bosses you pick. The webhook is stored outside our web root, used only for these posts, and disabled automatically if Discord rejects it three times. Remove it here any time or delete the webhook in Discord. To create one: channel settings, Integrations, Webhooks, New Webhook, Copy Webhook URL.</p></template><template data-topic-content="obs-overlay"><h2 class="tp-title" id="tpTitle">Aion 2 OBS Stream Overlay</h2><p>Put a live <strong>Aion 2 timer on your stream</strong>. The builder below writes a browser-source URL for OBS Studio, Streamlabs Desktop, StreamElements or any app that can load a web page, and shows you a scaled preview as you change options. Everything is carried in the URL, so the overlay needs no login and works on a second streaming PC.</p>
<h2>Overlay layouts</h2>
<ul><li><strong>Rift countdown</strong>: the big Spacetime Rift timer with portal open, active and closed states.</li><li><strong>Ticker bar</strong>: one line for the top or bottom edge at 1920 by 72, showing what is live now and the next few events.</li><li><strong>Next-up cards</strong>: a grid of upcoming events you choose.</li><li><strong>Checklist</strong>: your daily and weekly progress, synced with the main page.</li><li><strong>Twitch Chat: What To Play? (Wheel)</strong>: viewers type !spin in your Twitch chat and the class wheel spins on stream, with rigged spins, Wolves' Method, faction, region, P2W and yes/no wheels.</li><li><strong>Twitch Chat: What To Play? (Slot)</strong>: the same chat commands on the What To Play? slot machine, typed as !pull, with its picks added to the same running totals as the wheel.</li><li><strong>Twitch Chat: Aion 2 Trivia</strong>: your chat answers Aion 2 questions by typing A, B, C or D, faster right answers score more, and every channel keeps an all-time leaderboard.</li></ul>
<h2>Options that matter on stream</h2>
<p>Transparent, faint-card or text-only backgrounds, a size slider for crisp text at 1440p, text shadow for readability over gameplay, an accent colour to match your brand, times in the streaming PC's own time zone, 12 or 24-hour clock from your Settings, and an optional in-OBS sound alert with its own lead time. The overlay detects when it runs inside OBS, hides the cursor and scrollbars, and re-syncs the moment its scene becomes visible. Untick "Shutdown source when not visible" so the countdown keeps running between scenes.</p></template><template data-topic-content="classes"><h2 class="tp-title" id="tpTitle">Aion 2 Classes and Builds</h2><p>Aion 2 has <strong>9 playable classes</strong>: Gladiator, Templar, Assassin, Ranger, Sorcerer, Spiritmaster, Cleric, Chanter and Brawler. Every one of them is available to both factions and can be played as male or female, so picking a class never decides which side you land on. The panel above pulls each class straight from NCSOFT's official game data, with its skills, stigmas and specialisations under official English names.</p>
<h2>Picking a class</h2>
<p>We do not publish a tier list. Aion 2 balance moves with every patch, and a list written today is wrong by the next maintenance. What this page gives you instead is the actual data: the full skill list for each class, what each skill does at which level, the stigma options, and the specialisation trees, so you can judge a class on how it plays rather than on where somebody ranked it last month.</p>
<h2>Builds and planning</h2>
<p>The <a href="/planner/">Aion 2 Build Planner</a> lets you set a level, pick skills and stigmas, fit gear at any enhancement level and see the stat totals, then share the whole build as a link. The <a href="/calculator/">stat calculators</a> cover the maths behind combat power, and <a href="/db/">the database</a> holds every weapon, armour piece and accessory with stats at any enhancement level.</p>
<h2>Where the class data comes from</h2>
<p>Class, skill and specialisation data is mirrored from NCSOFT's official endpoints, not datamined or hand-typed, and refreshed daily. Skill descriptions come from NCSOFT's official Korean guidebook, machine translated. The official pages carry no damage numbers, ranges or cooldowns, so we do not show any &mdash; if you see those figures quoted elsewhere as official, they are not.</p></template><template data-topic-content="schedule"><h2 class="tp-title" id="tpTitle">Aion 2 Schedule Today</h2><p>This is the full <strong>Aion 2 schedule for today</strong>, converted from server time into your own time zone by your browser, so it stays correct through daylight-saving changes on both the Korea (UTC+9) and Taiwan (UTC+8) services.</p>
<h2>What repeats, and when</h2>
<ul><li><strong>Spacetime Rift</strong>: every 3 hours, 8 times a day, at 02:00, 05:00, 08:00, 11:00, 14:00, 17:00, 20:00 and 23:00 server time. The entry portal stays open about ten minutes.</li>
<li><strong>Daily reset</strong>: 05:00 server time.</li>
<li><strong>Weekly reset</strong>: Wednesday at 05:00 server time.</li>
<li><strong>World bosses, Shugo Festival, Dimensional Invasion and Beritra Air Raid</strong>: each on its own rotation, all listed above in your local time.</li></ul>
<h2>Why a schedule beats a single countdown</h2>
<p>One countdown tells you what is next. A day view tells you whether it is worth staying up &mdash; whether the rift at 23:00 lands before or after your reset, whether a boss and a rift collide, and what you would miss by logging off now. Pick your server in Settings (the gear button) and the whole day re-converts.</p>
<h2>Alerts</h2>
<p>If you would rather not watch a page, <a href="/discord-alerts/">Discord alerts</a> post to your server through a webhook and keep working with this page closed, and the <a href="/obs-overlay/">OBS overlay</a> puts the same schedule on stream.</p></template><dialog id="topicDialog" class="topic-dialog" aria-labelledby="tpTitle" aria-label="Guide"><div class="tp-head"><span class="eyebrow" style="margin:0">Guide</span><button class="icon-btn" id="tpClose" aria-label="Close" title="Close (Esc)"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><path d="M18 6 6 18M6 6l12 12"/></svg></button></div><div class="tp-body seo" id="tpBody" tabindex="0"></div><div class="tp-foot"><a class="btn small" id="tpOpen" href="/">Open full page</a><button class="btn small primary" id="tpDone">Close</button></div></dialog>
<template data-topic-content="about"><h2 class="tp-title">About HomelessGuyNABox</h2>
<p>HomelessGuyNABox is a charity music project. We run a 24/7 lo-fi radio stream on YouTube, along with daily study, focus and sleep mixes, set to calm, cozy scenes of people, animals and places. The music is royalty-free, so anyone can put it on while they study, work, game or wind down.</p>
<h2>How it is funded</h2>
<p>Aion 2 Timers is a free fan tool, with no account, subscription or paywall. HomelessGuyNABox covers its running costs, with help from visitors who choose to support it. Google ads may be added later to help; if they are, they will never appear in stream overlays or pop-out timer windows.</p>
<h2>Support the site</h2><p>Everything here stays free. Support given here goes directly to HomelessGuyNABox, the developer and maintainer of this site and every tool on it, as a thank you. You can give monthly on Patreon, or once or monthly on Ko-fi, and it does not unlock anything.</p><p style="display:flex;gap:8px;flex-wrap:wrap"><a class="btn small primary" href="https://www.patreon.com/Aion2Timers" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Support On Patreon</a> <a class="btn small btn-kofi" href="https://ko-fi.com/aion2timers" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Support With Ko-fi</a></p>
<h2>Why an Aion 2 timer?</h2>
<p>Because we play too, and the existing trackers were an hour off after the clocks changed. Building a correct one, and giving it away, fits what we do: make something useful and keep it free.</p>
<h2>Help us grow</h2>
<p>The single most useful thing you can do costs nothing. Open the channel, hit like on a mix, subscribe, and leave the stream playing while you grind. Watch time and subscribers are what turn a small channel into a funded one.</p>
<p><a class="btn primary" href="https://www.youtube.com/@homelessguynabox" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open the HomelessGuyNABox YouTube channel</a></p>
<p class="subtle">Like, subscribe, and listen. Thank you for being here.</p></template>

<!-- Region + timezone controls -->
<!-- Personal settings (#controls) live in #settingsSlots and show inside the Settings dialog (owner 2026-09-26) -->
<section class="card only-full" id="clocks">
  <div id="globalBanner" class="banner hidden">
    <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><path d="M12 9v4m0 4h.01M10.3 3.9 1.8 18a2 2 0 0 0 1.7 3h17a2 2 0 0 0 1.7-3L13.7 3.9a2 2 0 0 0-3.4 0z"/></svg>
    <div><b>Global servers open October 5, 2026 (Advance Access September 30).</b> NCSOFT has not published the server clock or event schedule for South America yet. Until it does, it uses the Korea/Taiwan clock schedule on its expected time zone (Brasília). You can override the assumed zone below. Treat these times as a placeholder and confirm in the live client.
      <div class="row" style="margin-top:8px"><label class="lbl" for="globalTz">Assumed server zone</label><select id="globalTz"></select></div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div id="maintBanner" class="banner maint hidden">
    <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><path d="M14.7 6.3a4 4 0 0 0-5.4 5.4L3 18l3 3 6.3-6.3a4 4 0 0 0 5.4-5.4l-2.4 2.4-2.1-2.1 2.4-2.4z"/></svg>
    <div id="maintBannerText"></div>
  </div>
  <!-- Notices (owner 2026-10-01): js/notice.js fills this from /notices.json for each notice's first hour, then the notice
       lives only in Featured > Notice. While it shows, renderMaint() puts the maintenance text inside it (#noticeMaint). -->
  <div id="noticeBanner" class="banner maint hidden" role="status">
    <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"/><path d="M12 8h.01M11 12h1v4h1"/></svg>
    <div class="on-body"><div id="noticeBody" data-no-i18n></div><div id="noticeMaint" class="hidden"></div></div>
  </div>
  <style>#globalBanner:not(.hidden)~#noticeBanner:not(.hidden),#maintBanner:not(.hidden)+#noticeBanner{margin-top:14px}
#noticeBanner{align-items:flex-start;border-color:rgba(251,191,36,.7);background:rgba(251,191,36,.16)}#noticeBanner>svg{margin-top:2px}
#noticeBanner .on-body{min-width:0;flex:1}
#noticeMaint{margin-top:12px;padding-top:10px;border-top:1px solid rgba(251,191,36,.45)}</style>
  <div class="clocks">
    <div class="clock"><div class="k">Your local time</div><div class="v mono" id="clkLocal">--:--:--</div><div class="subtle" id="clkLocalTz"></div></div>
    <div class="clock"><div class="k">Server time</div><div class="v mono" id="clkServer">--:--:--</div><div class="subtle" id="clkServerTz"></div></div>
    <div class="clock"><div class="k">Next daily reset</div><div class="v mono" id="clkDaily">--</div><div class="subtle">05:00 server time</div></div>
    <div class="clock"><div class="k">Next weekly reset</div><div class="v mono" id="clkWeekly">--</div><div class="subtle">Wednesday 05:00 server time</div></div>
  </div>
</section>

