<!-- Patch notes & notices -->
<section class="section only-full" id="patches">
  <div class="section-head">
    <div><div class="eyebrow">Official notices</div><h2>Patch notes and notices</h2></div>
    <div class="row"><span class="subtle" id="patchChecked"></span></div>
  </div>
  <details class="a2more"><summary class="btn small"><h2 class="a2sum" style="display:inline;font:inherit;margin:0;color:inherit;letter-spacing:inherit">About These Notices</h2></summary><div class="a2more-body"><p class="subtle">Collected automatically from NCSOFT's global, Korean and Taiwanese boards and AION2 Hub's English notes. Korean and Taiwanese notices are machine translated into English; open the original post for exact wording. Each link opens the original source in a new tab. Timer data on this page is updated by hand after a notice is verified.</p></div></details>
  <div class="filters" id="patchFilter"><button class="fbtn active" data-r="all">All</button><button class="fbtn" data-r="GLOBAL">Global (official)</button><button class="fbtn" data-r="ALL">English</button><button class="fbtn" data-r="KR">Korea</button><button class="fbtn" data-r="TW">Taiwan</button><button class="fbtn" type="button" data-r="hotfix">Hotfixes</button></div>
  <div class="card"><ul class="patch-list" id="patchList"></ul><button class="btn small" id="patchMore" hidden>Show more</button></div>
</section>

<!-- Launch -->
<section class="section only-full" id="launch">
  <div class="section-head"><div><div class="eyebrow">Global launch</div><h2>Countdown to the West</h2></div></div>
  <div class="grid cols-3" id="launchGrid"></div>
  <div class="banner info" style="margin-top:14px">
    <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"/><path d="M12 8h.01M11 12h1v4h1"/></svg>
    <div>Aion 2 launches globally on Monday, October 5, 2026 at 6:00 AM PDT / 9:00 AM EDT / 15:00 CEST (13:00 UTC), per the official Steam store page; the countdown above runs to that hour in your time zone. Founder's Pack Advance Access opened Wednesday, September 30 at 7:00 AM PDT / 16:00 CEST (14:00 UTC), one hour later than first planned per NCSOFT's official notice, and its pre-download opens Monday, September 28 at 6:00 AM PDT / 15:00 CEST (13:00 UTC), announced on the official AION 2 channel. Servers: North America, South America, Europe and Asia (Japan), on Steam and the PURPLE launcher.</div>
  </div>
</section>


<!-- Streamers / OBS -->
<section class="section only-full" id="obs">
  <div class="section-head"><div><div class="eyebrow">For streamers</div><h2>Stream overlay builder</h2></div><div class="subtle">Works in OBS Studio, Streamlabs Desktop, StreamElements and any browser-source app</div></div>
  <div class="card">
    <div class="builder">
      <div>
        <div class="opts">
          <div class="setting" style="grid-column:1/-1" id="obChWrap"><label class="lbl" for="obCh">Your channel <span class="obreq">Required</span></label><div class="row" style="gap:8px;flex-wrap:nowrap"><select id="obChPf" aria-label="Platform" style="flex:0 0 auto"><option value="twitch">Twitch</option><option value="youtube">YouTube</option><option value="kick">Kick</option><option value="tiktok">TikTok</option></select><input type="text" id="obCh" maxlength="60" placeholder="Your channel name" autocomplete="off" spellcheck="false" style="flex:1;min-width:0"></div><div class="subtle" id="obChNote" style="margin-top:4px;font-size:12px">Needed before you can copy the URL. We keep your channel name so we can see who streams with these tools. <a href="/streamers/#apply">Apply once on the Streamers page</a> with the same channel and you are featured automatically as soon as this overlay loads in OBS.</div></div>
          <div class="setting"><label class="lbl" for="obView">Layout</label><select id="obView"><option value="rift">Rift countdown (hero)</option><option value="bar">Ticker bar (one line: now + next)</option><option value="next">Next-up cards</option><option value="launch">Global launch ticker bar</option><option value="checklist">Daily / weekly checklist</option><option value="countdown">Custom countdown (your date or duration)</option><option value="whattoplay">What To Play? (slot or wheel)</option><option value="spinchat">Twitch Chat: What To Play? (Wheel)</option><option value="pullchat">Twitch Chat: What To Play? (Slot)</option><option value="dropchat">Twitch Chat: What To Play? (Plinko)</option><option value="triviachat">Twitch Chat: Aion 2 Trivia</option></select></div>
          <div class="setting"><label class="lbl" for="obRegion">Server</label><select id="obRegion"><option value="TW">Taiwan (UTC+8)</option><option value="KR">Korea (UTC+9)</option><option value="NAW">NA West</option><option value="NAE">NA East</option><option value="SA">South America</option><option value="EU">Europe</option><option value="JP">Japan</option></select></div>
          <div class="setting"><label class="lbl" for="obBg">Background</label><select id="obBg"><option value="dark">Dark card</option><option value="transparent">Transparent, faint card</option><option value="none">Transparent, no card (text only)</option><option value="solid">Solid dark</option></select></div>
          <div class="setting" id="obWtpWrap" hidden><div class="lbl g">Classes in the pool <span class="links2" style="display:inline-flex;gap:6px;margin-left:8px;vertical-align:middle"><button type="button" class="btn small" id="obWtpAll">All</button><button type="button" class="btn small" id="obWtpNone">None</button></span></div><div id="obWtpCls" class="links2" style="gap:6px"></div><div class="note">Untick a class to keep it out of the spin. These travel with the overlay URL, so the overlay spins from exactly this list.</div></div><div class="setting" id="obWtpOptWrap" hidden><div class="lbl g">What To Play? options</div><label class="lbl" for="obWtpView">Style</label><select id="obWtpView"><option value="slot">Slot machine</option><option value="wheel">Spinning wheel</option><option value="plinko">Plinko board</option></select><label class="lbl" for="obWtpRegion" style="margin-top:8px">Region</label><select id="obWtpRegion"><option value="all">KR / TW (every class)</option><option value="global">Global launch classes only</option></select><label class="chk"><input type="checkbox" id="obWtpWolves"> Wolves’ Method</label><label class="chk"><input type="checkbox" id="obWtpCard" checked> Show the class card</label><label class="chk"><input type="checkbox" id="obWtpFilters"> Hide the class buttons on the overlay <span class="note">(cleaner for stream)</span></label></div><div class="setting" id="obSpinWrap" hidden style="grid-column:1/-1"><style>#obSpinWrap label.lbl{display:block;margin-bottom:4px}#obSpinWrap input[type=text],#obSpinWrap input[type=number],#obSpinWrap select{width:100%}</style><div class="lbl g" data-spm="wheel">Twitch Chat: What To Play? (Wheel)</div><div class="lbl g" data-spm="slot" hidden>Twitch Chat: What To Play? (Slot)</div><div class="lbl g" data-spm="plinko" hidden>Twitch Chat: What To Play? (Plinko)</div><div class="lbl g" data-spm="trivia" hidden>Twitch Chat: Aion 2 Trivia</div><div class="note" style="margin-bottom:8px" data-spm="wheel">Viewers type <code>!spin</code> in your Twitch chat and the wheel spins on stream. The overlay reads your chat itself, so only the channel name is required. For YouTube or Kick chat through a bot, build the command on the <a href="/streamers/#spinwheel">Streamer Kit</a>.</div><div class="note" style="margin-bottom:8px" data-spm="slot" hidden>Viewers type <code>!pull</code> in your Twitch chat and the What To Play? slot machine pulls on stream. Same commands and options as the wheel, and its picks count toward the same totals. About 3 pulls in 100 lands on the HomelessGuyNABox logo for a Jackpot Spin: three reels, Whale classes and piles of Quna on the result card. About 1 finished spin, pull or drop in 20 ends with Game Mode Change!: the overlay spins Wheel, Slot and Plinko against each other and switches if another game wins, carrying on with the queue there, with !spin, !pull and !drop all working from then on. You, your mods and HomelessGuyInABox can also call one with !gamechange. About 1 viewer turn in 20 an Assassin stabs the viewer in the back and hands the turn to another chatter; you, your mods and HomelessGuyInABox can send one with !stab, and it hits the next viewer turn. <span>New subscribers and sub gifters jump to the front of the queue with a jackpot turn on every Global class (one turn per gifter, however many subs they gift).</span> <span>Everyone who receives a gifted sub is added to the queue for a normal turn.</span> The overlay reads your chat itself, so only the channel name is required. For YouTube or Kick chat through a bot, build the command on the <a href="/streamers/#slotmachine">Streamer Kit</a>.</div><div class="note" style="margin-bottom:8px" data-spm="plinko" hidden>Viewers type <code>!drop</code> in your Twitch chat and a ball bounces down the What To Play? Plinko board into one of all 8 Global classes on stream. The other commands and options work as on the wheel, and its picks count toward the same totals. About 3 drops in 100 are a Jackpot Drop with a gold ball and Whale classes. Plinko is new, so it is not part of Game Mode Change yet. The overlay reads your chat itself, so only the channel name is required. For YouTube or Kick chat through a bot, build the command on the <a href="/streamers/#plinko">Streamer Kit</a>.</div><div class="note" style="margin-bottom:8px" data-spm="trivia" hidden>Your chat plays Aion 2 trivia together: a question with four answers shows on stream and viewers answer by typing <code>a</code> <code>b</code> <code>c</code> or <code>d</code> in chat. Faster right answers score more, and three right in a row scores half as much again. Every channel keeps an all-time leaderboard. Questions come from the site’s own class, skill, boss and dungeon data, in the language the site is set to. The overlay reads your chat itself, so only the channel name is required.</div><div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fill,minmax(210px,1fr));gap:10px"><div><label class="lbl" for="obSpTwitch">Twitch channel (required)</label><input type="text" id="obSpTwitch" placeholder="yourchannel" autocomplete="off" spellcheck="false" maxlength="25"></div><div><label class="lbl" for="obSpCmd">Command</label><input type="text" id="obSpCmd" value="!spin" spellcheck="false" maxlength="20"></div><div><label class="lbl" for="obSpWho"><span data-spm="wheel">Who may spin</span><span data-spm="slot" hidden>Who may pull</span><span data-spm="plinko" hidden>Who may drop</span></label><select id="obSpWho"><option value="all">Everyone</option><option value="subs">Subscribers, VIPs and mods</option><option value="mods">Mods only</option></select></div><div><label class="lbl" for="obSpCd">Per-viewer cooldown (seconds)</label><input type="number" id="obSpCd" value="1" min="0" max="3600"></div><div><label class="lbl" for="obSpSize"><span data-spm="wheel">Wheel size (pixels)</span><span data-spm="slot" hidden>Slot machine width (pixels)</span><span data-spm="plinko" hidden>Plinko board size (pixels)</span></label><input type="number" id="obSpSize" value="560" min="240" max="1400"></div><div><label class="lbl" for="obSpIdle"><span data-spm="wheel">Between spins</span><span data-spm="slot" hidden>Between pulls</span><span data-spm="plinko" hidden>Between drops</span></label><select id="obSpIdle"><option value="show">Show it</option><option value="hide">Hide it</option></select></div><div><label class="lbl" for="obSpBg">Background</label><select id="obSpBg"><option value="transparent">Transparent</option><option value="black">Black</option></select></div><div><label class="lbl" for="obSpRig"><span data-spm="wheel">Rigged spin class (!spin rigged)</span><span data-spm="slot" hidden>Rigged pull class (!pull rigged)</span><span data-spm="plinko" hidden>Rigged drop class (!drop rigged)</span></label><select id="obSpRig"><option value="templar">Templar</option><option value="gladiator">Gladiator</option><option value="assassin">Assassin</option><option value="ranger" selected>Ranger</option><option value="sorcerer">Sorcerer</option><option value="spiritmaster">Spiritmaster</option><option value="cleric">Cleric</option><option value="chanter">Chanter</option><option value="brawler">Brawler (KR/TW)</option></select></div><div><label class="lbl" for="obSpRiggers"><span data-spm="wheel">Mods who may rig and ask yes/no (names, comma separated)</span><span data-spm="slot" hidden>Mods who may rig and ask yes/no (names, comma separated)</span><span data-spm="plinko" hidden>Mods who may rig and ask yes/no (names, comma separated)</span><span data-spm="trivia" hidden>Extra people who may run trivia (names, comma separated)</span></label><input type="text" id="obSpRiggers" maxlength="300" placeholder="Twitch mods are detected automatically" spellcheck="false"></div><div><label class="lbl" for="obSpBy">Name on the Rigged by stamp</label><input type="text" id="obSpBy" maxlength="25" placeholder="your channel name"></div><div><label class="lbl" for="obSpPre"><span data-spm="wheel">Countdown before the spin (seconds)</span><span data-spm="slot" hidden>Countdown before the pull (seconds)</span><span data-spm="plinko" hidden>Countdown before the drop (seconds)</span></label><input type="number" id="obSpPre" value="3" min="0" max="15"></div><div><label class="lbl" for="obSpHold">Result stays on screen (seconds)</label><input type="number" id="obSpHold" value="5" min="2" max="60"></div><div><label class="lbl" for="obSpRegional">Brawler (Korea and Taiwan only)</label><select id="obSpRegional"><option value="0">Denied with a stamp (Global)</option><option value="1">Allowed</option></select></div><div><label class="lbl" for="obSpTally"><span data-spm="wheel">Wheel totals on the card</span><span data-spm="slot" hidden>Totals on the card (shared with the wheel)</span><span data-spm="plinko" hidden>Totals on the card (shared with the wheel)</span></label><select id="obSpTally"><option value="1">Show</option><option value="0">Hide (still counted)</option></select></div></div><div data-spm="trivia" hidden style="margin-top:10px"><div class="lbl" style="margin-bottom:4px">Question topics</div><div id="obTvCats" class="links2" style="gap:6px;margin-bottom:10px"><label class="chk"><input type="checkbox" value="classes" checked> Classes</label><label class="chk"><input type="checkbox" value="skills" checked> Skills</label><label class="chk"><input type="checkbox" value="bosses" checked> Field bosses</label><label class="chk"><input type="checkbox" value="dungeons" checked> Dungeons</label><label class="chk"><input type="checkbox" value="launch" checked> Global launch</label></div><div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fill,minmax(210px,1fr));gap:10px"><div><label class="lbl" for="obTvDiff">Difficulty</label><select id="obTvDiff"><option value="0">Mixed</option><option value="1">Beginner</option><option value="2">Veteran</option></select></div><div><label class="lbl" for="obTvN">Questions per round</label><input type="number" id="obTvN" value="10" min="3" max="30"></div><div><label class="lbl" for="obTvTime">Seconds to answer</label><input type="number" id="obTvTime" value="20" min="10" max="60"></div><div><label class="lbl" for="obTvGap">Seconds the answer shows</label><input type="number" id="obTvGap" value="8" min="4" max="30"></div><div><label class="lbl" for="obTvAuto">Quiet chat: one question every (minutes, 0 = off)</label><input type="number" id="obTvAuto" value="5" min="0" max="60"></div><div><label class="lbl" for="obTvSize">Card width (pixels)</label><input type="number" id="obTvSize" value="640" min="360" max="1400"></div><div><label class="lbl" for="obTvKr">Korea and Taiwan questions (Brawler)</label><select id="obTvKr"><option value="0">Leave out (Global)</option><option value="1">Include</option></select></div></div></div><div class="note" style="margin-top:8px" data-spm="trivia" hidden>Chat commands: <code>!a</code> to <code>!d</code> (or <code>!1</code> to <code>!4</code>) to answer, only the first answer counts, and <code>!trivia top</code> for the channel’s all-time top 5. For you and your mods: <code>!trivia start</code> for a round, <code>!trivia start bosses 5</code> for a round of 5 boss questions, <code>!trivia start beginner</code> or <code>!trivia start veteran</code> for one difficulty across every topic, <code>!trivia next</code> for a single question, <code>!trivia skip</code> and <code>!trivia stop</code>. Untick "Shutdown source when not visible" in OBS so trivia keeps listening between scenes.</div><div class="note" style="margin-top:8px" data-spm="wheel">Chat commands: <code>!spin glad, ranger, sm</code>, <code>!spin all</code>, <code>-cleric</code> to drop a class, <code>wolves</code> for elimination spins, <code>!spin faction</code>, <code>!spin region</code>, <code>!spin server</code>, <code>!spin p2w</code>, and for you and your mods <code>!spin rigged</code>, <code>!spin @viewer</code> and <code>!spin yes/no &lt;question&gt;</code>. After one quiet minute the wheel picks a viewer from your chat and spins a random wheel for them on its own, so it never sits still. Untick "Shutdown source when not visible" in OBS so the wheel keeps listening between scenes.</div><div class="note" style="margin-top:8px" data-spm="slot" hidden>Chat commands: <code>!pull glad, ranger, sm</code>, <code>!pull all</code>, <code>-cleric</code> to drop a class, <code>wolves</code> for elimination pulls, <code>!pull faction</code>, <code>!pull region</code>, <code>!pull p2w</code>, and for you and your mods <code>!pull rigged</code>, <code>!pull @viewer</code> and <code>!pull yes/no &lt;question&gt;</code>. After one quiet minute the slot machine picks a viewer from your chat and pulls a random reel for them on its own, so it never sits still. Untick "Shutdown source when not visible" in OBS so the slot machine keeps listening between scenes.</div><div class="note" style="margin-top:8px" data-spm="plinko" hidden>Chat commands: <code>!drop glad, ranger, sm</code>, <code>!drop all</code>, <code>-cleric</code> to drop a class, <code>wolves</code> for elimination drops, <code>!drop faction</code>, <code>!drop region</code>, <code>!drop server</code>, <code>!drop p2w</code>, and for you and your mods <code>!drop rigged</code>, <code>!drop @viewer</code> and <code>!drop yes/no &lt;question&gt;</code>. After one quiet minute the board picks a viewer from your chat and drops a ball for them on its own, so it never sits still. Untick "Shutdown source when not visible" in OBS so the board keeps listening between scenes.</div></div><div class="setting" id="obCdWrap" hidden style="grid-column:1/-1"><style>#obCdWrap label.lbl{display:block;margin-bottom:4px}#obCdWrap input[type=text],#obCdWrap input[type=datetime-local],#obCdWrap select{width:100%}#obCdWrap input.bad{border-color:var(--danger,#f87171)}</style><div class="lbl g">Custom countdown</div><div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fill,minmax(210px,1fr));gap:10px"><div><label class="lbl" for="obCdMode">Count down</label><select id="obCdMode"><option value="dur">From a duration (like 10:00)</option><option value="date">To a date and time</option></select></div><div data-cdm="dur"><label class="lbl" for="obCdDur">Duration (h:mm:ss, mm:ss or minutes)</label><input type="text" id="obCdDur" value="10:00" maxlength="12" autocomplete="off" spellcheck="false" inputmode="numeric"></div><div data-cdm="dur"><label class="lbl" for="obCdStart">Starts</label><select id="obCdStart"><option value="load">When the source loads (a refresh restarts it)</option><option value="copy">When I copy the URL (a refresh keeps going)</option><option value="at">At a time I pick</option></select></div><div data-cdm="when"><label class="lbl" for="obCdWhen"><span data-cdw="date">Date and time</span><span data-cdw="at" hidden>Start date and time</span></label><input type="datetime-local" id="obCdWhen"></div><div data-cdm="when"><label class="lbl" for="obCdTz">Time zone of that time</label><select id="obCdTz"></select></div><div><label class="lbl" for="obCdLabel">Label</label><input type="text" id="obCdLabel" maxlength="80" placeholder="Stream starts in" autocomplete="off"></div><div><label class="lbl" for="obCdAfter">At zero</label><select id="obCdAfter"><option value="text">Show the end text</option><option value="zero">Stay on 00:00</option><option value="up">Count up (time since zero)</option><option value="hide">Hide the overlay</option></select></div><div data-cda="text"><label class="lbl" for="obCdEnd">End text</label><input type="text" id="obCdEnd" maxlength="80" value="Starting now" autocomplete="off"></div><div><label class="lbl" for="obCdSound">Sound at zero</label><select id="obCdSound"><option value="">No sound</option><option value="double">Double beep</option><option value="chime">Triple chime</option><option value="asc">Ascending</option><option value="alarm">Alert tone</option><option value="pulse">Pulse</option><option value="soft">Soft bell</option><option value="cash">Cha-Ching</option></select></div><div><label class="lbl" for="obCdColor">Number colour</label><div class="row"><input type="color" id="obCdColor" value="#ffffff" style="width:44px;height:36px;border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:8px;background:var(--surface);padding:2px"><button type="button" class="btn small" id="obCdColorReset">Default</button></div></div></div><label class="chk" style="margin-top:8px"><input type="checkbox" id="obCdAt"> Show the date and time under the countdown</label><div class="note" id="obCdWarn" hidden>That time has already passed, so the overlay starts at zero.</div><details class="a2more" style="margin-top:6px"><summary class="btn small">More</summary><div class="a2more-body"><p class="subtle">The date is saved in the URL as one exact moment, so viewers and streaming PCs in any time zone count down to the same second, and daylight saving is handled for you. "When I copy the URL" stamps the start time when you press Copy URL or Open, so refreshing the source in OBS does not restart it. Copy a fresh URL to start again. Sound at zero plays only when the overlay is running as it reaches zero. Tick Control audio via OBS to hear it on stream.</p></div></details></div><div class="setting" id="obAutoWrap" hidden><label class="lbl" for="obAuto">Spin</label><select id="obAuto"><option value="1">Spin when the source loads or refreshes</option><option value="0">Wait for a click or the Space key</option></select><div class="note">Refreshing the browser source in OBS is the easiest way to spin again on stream.</div></div><div class="setting"><label class="lbl" for="obScale">Size <span id="obScaleLbl">100%</span></label><input type="range" id="obScale" min="50" max="250" step="5" value="100"></div>
          <div class="setting" id="obNowWrap" hidden><div class="lbl g">Ticker bar</div><label class="chk"><input type="checkbox" id="obNow"> Hide the &ldquo;Now&rdquo; card <span class="note">(show only what is coming up)</span></label></div><div class="setting"><label class="lbl" for="obN">Cards to show</label><select id="obN"><option value="3">3</option><option value="4" selected>4</option><option value="5">5</option><option value="6">6</option><option value="8">8</option><option value="10">10</option></select></div>
          <div class="setting"><label class="lbl" for="obTz">Time zone shown</label><select id="obTz" class="oblocked" disabled><option value="">Streaming PC's own</option></select><div class="subtle oblock-note">Overlays always use the streaming PC's own time zone.</div></div>
          <div class="setting"><label class="lbl" for="obFmt">Clock</label><select id="obFmt" class="oblocked" disabled><option value="12">12-hour</option><option value="24">24-hour</option></select><div class="subtle oblock-note">Set by the Clock choice in Settings. <button type="button" class="btn small" data-open-settings>Settings</button></div></div>
          <div class="setting"><label class="lbl" for="obAccent">Accent colour</label><div class="row"><input type="color" id="obAccent" value="#a78bfa" style="width:44px;height:36px;border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:8px;background:var(--surface);padding:2px"><button class="btn small" id="obAccentReset">Default</button></div></div>
          <div class="setting" style="grid-column:1/-1"><div class="lbl g">Options</div>
            <div class="row" style="gap:14px">
              <label class="toggle"><input type="checkbox" id="obCompact"> Compact (numbers only)</label>
              <label class="toggle"><input type="checkbox" id="obHead"> Hide section titles</label>
              <label class="toggle"><input type="checkbox" id="obShadow" checked> Text shadow (readable over video)</label>
              <label class="toggle"><input type="checkbox" id="obBrand" checked> Small site credit</label>
              <label class="toggle"><input type="checkbox" id="obSound"> Sound alert in OBS</label>
              <select id="obLead" class="hidden" title="Sound alert lead time" style="min-height:32px;padding:4px 8px;font-size:13px"><option value="1">1 min before</option><option value="3">3 min before</option><option value="5" selected>5 min before</option><option value="10">10 min before</option></select>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="setting" style="grid-column:1/-1" id="obEvWrap"><div class="lbl g">Events in the overlay</div><div class="evpick" id="obEv"></div></div>
        </div>
        <div class="urlbox"><label class="sr-only" for="obUrl">Overlay URL</label><input type="text" id="obUrl" readonly><button class="btn primary" id="obCopy">Copy URL</button><button class="btn" id="obOpen">Open</button></div>
        <div class="subtle" style="margin-top:8px">Suggested source size: <b id="obSize" class="mono">520 × 300</b>. Overlays do not need a login and carry every setting in the URL, so they work on a different PC.</div>
      </div>
      <div>
        <div class="preview" id="obPreviewBox"><iframe id="obPreview" title="Overlay preview" loading="lazy"></iframe><span class="sz" id="obPreviewSz"></span></div>
        <details open style="margin-top:12px"><summary>Add it to OBS Studio</summary><div class="body">
          <ol class="steps"><li>Sources → <b>+</b> → <b>Browser</b> → name it, OK.</li><li>Paste the URL above. Set <b>Width / Height</b> to the suggested size (you can resize the source afterwards; use the Size slider here for crisp text instead of stretching).</li><li>Leave <b>Custom CSS</b> as it is. The default rule already makes the page background transparent.</li><li><b>Untick "Shutdown source when not visible"</b> so the countdown keeps running between scenes. <b>"Refresh browser when scene becomes active"</b> is safe either way; the overlay carries no state.</li><li>If you enabled the sound alert, tick <b>Control audio via OBS</b> and mix it like any other source.</li></ol>
          Streamlabs Desktop: same steps under <b>Sources → Browser Source</b>. StreamElements overlay editor: <b>Add widget → Static / Custom → Custom widget</b>, then paste the URL in an iframe, or use the browser source in your streaming app.
        </div></details>
        <details><summary>Tips for a clean overlay</summary><div class="body">
          <ul><li>Use "Transparent, no card" plus text shadow for a floating timer over gameplay; "Dark card" when it sits on a panel.</li><li>The Ticker bar layout is built for the top or bottom edge at 1920 × 60 to 1920 × 80.</li><li>OBS renders at your canvas resolution. A 1080p canvas with the overlay at 100% is right for 1080p output; scale to 150% if you stream at 1440p or larger.</li><li>The overlay detects when it runs inside OBS and hides the cursor and scrollbars. When the scene becomes visible it re-syncs immediately.</li><li>Times always follow the streaming PC's own clock and time zone. 12-hour or 24-hour comes from the Clock in Settings.</li><li>Change the server or event list later by editing the URL. Nothing is stored on our side.</li></ul>
        </div></details>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- Settings -->
<section class="section only-full" id="settings">
  <div class="section-head"><div><div class="eyebrow">Alerts</div><h2>Alert settings</h2></div><div class="subtle">Saved in this browser only</div></div>
  <div class="card">
    <div class="settings">
      <div class="setting"><div class="lbl g">Master switch</div><label class="toggle"><input type="checkbox" id="setMaster" checked> Alerts on</label></div>
      <div class="setting"><label class="lbl" for="setTone">Sound</label><label class="toggle"><input type="checkbox" id="setSound"> Play sound</label>
        <select id="setTone"><option value="double">Double beep</option><option value="chime">Triple chime</option><option value="asc">Ascending</option><option value="alarm">Alert tone</option><option value="pulse">Pulse</option><option value="soft">Soft bell</option><option value="cash">Cha-Ching</option></select></div>
      <div class="setting"><label class="lbl" for="setVol">Volume <span id="volLabel">60%</span></label><input type="range" id="setVol" min="0" max="100" value="60"></div>
      <div class="setting"><label class="lbl" for="setRepeat">Repeat sound</label><select id="setRepeat"><option value="1">Once</option><option value="3">3 times</option><option value="6">6 times</option><option value="0">Until dismissed</option></select></div>
      <div class="setting"><div class="lbl g">Default lead times</div><div id="setLeads"></div><span class="subtle">Each event card can override this.</span><span class="subtle">Every lead time fires once per occurrence. Discord alerts use the longest one.</span></div>
      <div class="setting"><div class="lbl g">Final countdown</div><label class="toggle"><input type="checkbox" id="setCd10"> Beep the last 10 seconds</label><label class="toggle"><input type="checkbox" id="setCdVoice"> Speak the numbers</label><span class="subtle">Each event can turn this on or off in its details.</span></div>
      <div class="setting"><div class="lbl g">Custom timers</div><div class="row"><button class="btn small" id="ctExport" type="button">Export</button><button class="btn small" id="ctImport" type="button">Import</button><input type="file" id="ctImportFile" accept="application/json,.json" hidden></div><span class="subtle" id="ctCount"></span></div>
      <div class="setting"><div class="lbl g">Also alert</div><label class="toggle"><input type="checkbox" id="setAtStart" checked> At the moment it starts</label><label class="toggle"><input type="checkbox" id="setAtClose" checked> 1 min before the rift portal closes</label></div>
      <div class="setting"><div class="lbl g">Browser notifications</div><button class="btn small" id="notifyBtn">Enable</button><span class="subtle" id="notifyState"></span></div>
      <div class="setting"><div class="lbl g">Tab title</div><label class="toggle"><input type="checkbox" id="setTitle" checked> Show next rift countdown in the tab title</label></div>
      <div class="setting"><div class="lbl g" id="qhLbl">Quiet hours (local)</div><div class="row"><select id="quietFrom" aria-labelledby="qhLbl"></select><span class="subtle" id="qhTo">to</span><select id="quietTo" aria-labelledby="qhLbl qhTo"></select></div><span class="subtle">No sound or notifications inside this window. Same value = off.</span></div>
      <div class="setting" id="panelSetting"><div class="lbl g">Main page sections</div><div class="panel-toggles" id="panelToggles"></div><span class="subtle">Pick what shows on the home page. Everything stays reachable from the menu either way.</span></div><div class="setting"><label class="lbl" for="setFmt">Time format</label><select id="setFmt"><option value="12">12-hour</option><option value="24">24-hour</option></select></div>
    </div>
    <div class="row" style="margin-top:16px">
      <button class="btn" id="testAlertBtn">Test full alert</button>
      <button class="btn" id="stopSoundBtn">Stop sound</button>
      <button class="btn" id="exportBtn">Copy settings link</button>
      <span class="subtle">Tip: keep this tab open. Browsers only fire timers and notifications for pages that are loaded, and some phones pause background tabs.</span>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>


<!-- Discord -->
<section class="section only-full" id="discord">
  <div class="section-head"><div><div class="eyebrow">Discord</div><h2>Alerts in your Discord server</h2></div><div class="subtle">Fires even when this page is closed</div></div>
  <div class="card">
    <div class="grid cols-2" style="align-items:start">
      <div>
        <p class="muted" style="margin:0 0 12px">Three steps, about a minute. Our alert server posts to your channel through a webhook, so it keeps working with this page closed, and every reader sees the times in their own zone. No bot to invite.</p>
        <div class="dc-step"><div class="dc-n">1</div><div class="dc-b">
          <div class="lbl g">Create a webhook in Discord</div>
          <ol class="dc-ol"><li>Open the channel's settings (gear) &rarr; <b>Integrations</b> &rarr; <b>Webhooks</b> &rarr; <b>New Webhook</b>.</li><li>Click <b>Copy Webhook URL</b>, then press <b>Paste</b> below.</li></ol>
          <details class="a2more"><summary class="btn small">More</summary><div class="a2more-body"><p class="subtle">You need the Manage Webhooks permission in that server. On a phone, long-press the channel, then Edit Channel &rarr; Integrations. The webhook's name and picture do not matter: our messages use their own. Deleting the webhook in Discord stops the alerts instantly.</p></div></details>
          <div class="setting" style="margin-top:8px"><label class="lbl" for="dcWebhook">Webhook URL</label><div class="dc-in"><input type="text" id="dcWebhook" placeholder="https://discord.com/api/webhooks/1234567890/abc..." autocomplete="off" spellcheck="false"><button type="button" class="btn small" id="dcPaste">Paste</button></div><div class="note dc-check" id="dcHookCheck" aria-live="polite"></div></div>
        </div></div>
        <div class="dc-step"><div class="dc-n">2</div><div class="dc-b">
          <div class="lbl g">Choose what to send</div>
          <div class="dc-bar"><label class="lbl" for="dcRegion">Server</label><select id="dcRegion"></select><span class="dc-quick"><button type="button" class="btn small" data-dcq="rec">Recommended</button><button type="button" class="btn small" data-dcq="all">All</button><button type="button" class="btn small" data-dcq="none">None</button></span></div>
          <div class="dc-evs" id="dcEvList"></div>
          <div class="note" id="dcEvHint"></div>
        <div class="settings" style="margin:12px 0">
          <div class="setting"><label class="lbl" for="dcMention">Ping</label><select id="dcMention"><option value="none">Nobody</option><option value="here">@here</option><option value="everyone">@everyone</option><option value="role">A role (enter ID)</option></select><input type="text" id="dcRole" class="hidden" title="Role ID" placeholder="Role ID, e.g. 1234567890123456789" inputmode="numeric"><div class="note dc-check" id="dcRoleCheck"></div></div>
          <div class="setting"><div class="lbl g">Include</div><label class="toggle"><input type="checkbox" id="dcLaunch" checked> Global launch milestones (30 min before)</label></div>
          <div class="setting"><div class="lbl g" aria-hidden="true">&nbsp;</div><label class="toggle"><input type="checkbox" id="dcBoard"> Live timer board: one message in the channel that keeps itself up to date</label><div class="note">Pin it in Discord so it stays on top.</div></div>
          <div class="setting"><div class="lbl g" aria-hidden="true">&nbsp;</div><label class="toggle"><input type="checkbox" id="dcFb"> Field boss respawns on my server, the moment the AbyssLogs DPS Meter sees a boss come back</label><div class="note" id="dcFbHint"></div><details class="a2more" id="dcFbPick"><summary class="btn small"><h2 class="a2sum" style="display:inline;font:inherit;margin:0;color:inherit;letter-spacing:inherit">Choose Bosses</h2></summary><div class="a2more-body"><div class="dc-quick" style="margin-bottom:6px"><button type="button" class="btn small" data-dcfb="all">All</button><button type="button" class="btn small" data-dcfb="none">None</button></div><div class="dc-evs" id="dcFbList"></div></div></details></div>
          <div class="setting"><div class="lbl g" aria-hidden="true">&nbsp;</div><label class="toggle"><input type="checkbox" id="dcNotes"> Patch notes and hotfixes, posted when they go up</label></div>
          <div class="setting"><div class="lbl g" aria-hidden="true">&nbsp;</div><label class="toggle"><input type="checkbox" id="dcHotfixOnly"> Hotfixes only, skip the regular update notes</label></div>
          <div class="setting"><div class="lbl g" aria-hidden="true">&nbsp;</div><label class="toggle"><input type="checkbox" id="dcNotesOnly"> Send nothing but notes, no event timers or launch milestones</label><div class="note" id="dcNotesHint"></div></div>
        </div>
        </div></div>
        <div class="dc-step"><div class="dc-n">3</div><div class="dc-b">
        <div class="lbl g" style="margin-bottom:8px">Save, and check your channel for the test message</div>
        <div class="row">
          <button class="btn primary" id="dcSave">Save and send test</button>
          <button class="btn" id="dcTest">Send test again</button>
          <button class="btn" id="dcRemove">Remove</button>
        </div>
        <div id="dcStatus" class="subtle" style="margin-top:10px"></div>
        <div id="dcSummary" class="banner ok hidden" style="margin-top:12px"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><path d="M20 6 9 17l-5-5"/></svg><div></div></div>
        </div></div>
      </div>
      <div>
        <div class="dc-prevhead"><div class="lbl g">Preview</div><select id="dcPrevKind" aria-label="Preview"><option value="alert">Next alert</option><option value="board">Live timer board</option><option value="test">Test message</option></select></div>
        <div class="dc-msg" id="dcPreview" aria-live="off"></div>
        <div class="dc-bot">
          <div><b>Prefer a bot?</b> <span class="subtle">Invite the Aion 2 Timers bot and ask it in any channel: <code>!timer rift</code>, <code>!timer shugo naw</code>, <code>!timers</code>, <code>!timer play</code>.</span></div>
          <a class="btn small btn-discord" href="https://discord.com/oauth2/authorize?client_id=1554820970437673011&amp;permissions=84992&amp;scope=bot" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Invite The Bot</a>
          <details class="a2more"><summary class="btn small">More</summary><div class="a2more-body"><p class="subtle">The bot answers on request with a live countdown card; the webhook on the left posts by itself before each event. Use either or both. The bot only asks to view the channel, send messages, embed links and read message history. <code>!timer help</code> lists every timer and region.</p></div></details>
        </div>
        <details><summary>What gets sent, and when</summary><div class="body">One message per event occurrence, at the lead time you pick in step 2. The live board is a single message that is edited when the next time changes, instead of a new post. The rift message includes the portal-close time. Hourly events post every hour, so consider leaving Shugo Festival and Dimensional Invasion off for Discord unless your server wants that volume. Discord allows 30 messages a minute per webhook; we stay well under that.</div></details>
        <details><summary>Privacy</summary><div class="body">The webhook URL is stored on our server outside the web root and used only to post these alerts. It is never shown in full again on this page. Remove it here at any time, or delete the webhook in Discord. Webhooks that return errors three times in a row are disabled automatically.</div></details>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section only-full fullsched" id="fullschedule"><div class="section-head"><div><div class="eyebrow">Server schedule</div><h2>Aion 2 event schedule in server time</h2></div><div class="subtle">Korea UTC+9, Taiwan UTC+8. Verified 2026-09-30</div></div><div class="card tbl-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Event</th><th>Type</th><th>Server time</th><th>Lasts</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spacetime Rift</td><td>Rift</td><td>Daily 02:00, 05:00, 08:00, 11:00, 14:00, 17:00, 20:00, 23:00</td><td>1 h</td></tr><tr><td>Spacetime Rift Domination</td><td>PvP</td><td>Mon, Thu, Sat 20:00, 23:00</td><td>20 min</td></tr><tr><td>Abyss Rift Zone</td><td>PvP battlefield</td><td>Tue, Thu 22:00</td><td>35 min</td></tr><tr><td>Artifact Conquest (Abyss)</td><td>Abyss</td><td>Wed, Sat 21:30</td><td>30 min</td></tr><tr><td>Post-Conquest Abyss bosses</td><td>Abyss boss</td><td>Wed, Sat 21:45</td><td>30 min</td></tr><tr><td>Watcher Kaira</td><td>Abyss boss</td><td>Daily 01:00, 05:00, 09:00, 13:00, 17:00, 21:00</td><td>instant</td></tr><tr><td>Enraged Guardian Lord Nahma</td><td>Abyss boss</td><td>Fri, Sun 22:00, 22:30, 23:00</td><td>30 min</td></tr><tr><td>Abyss Battlefield hours</td><td>Abyss</td><td>Daily 11:00, 20:00</td><td>3 h / 2 h</td></tr><tr><td>Shugo Festival</td><td>Minigames</td><td>Every hour at :00</td><td>5 min</td></tr><tr><td>Dimensional Invasion</td><td>World event</td><td>Every hour at :30</td><td>15 min</td></tr><tr><td>Beritra Air Raid</td><td>Boss raid</td><td>Every hour at :30</td><td>15 min</td></tr><tr><td>Black Cloud Merchant refresh</td><td>Shop</td><td>Every hour at :00</td><td>1 h</td></tr><tr><td>Daily reset</td><td>Reset</td><td>Daily 05:00</td><td>instant</td></tr><tr><td>Weekly reset</td><td>Reset</td><td>Wed 05:00</td><td>instant</td></tr></tbody></table><p class="subtle" style="margin:12px 0 0">Same clock on both live services; the Korea server runs one hour ahead of Taiwan in real time. The cards above convert every row to your local time.</p></div></section>
<section class="section only-full faq" id="faq"><div class="section-head"><div><div class="eyebrow">FAQ</div><h2>Frequently asked questions</h2></div></div><div class="grid cols-2"><button class="dcard" type="button" data-label="FAQ"><span class="dcard-t">When does the next Spacetime Rift open in Aion 2?</span><span class="dcard-c">+</span><span class="dcard-body hidden">Spacetime Rifts open every 3 hours, 8 times a day, at 02:00, 05:00, 08:00, 11:00, 14:00, 17:00, 20:00 and 23:00 server time. The entry portal stays open about 10 minutes and the rift window lasts up to 1 hour. The countdown at the top of this page converts the next opening to your local time.</span></button><button class="dcard" type="button" data-label="FAQ"><span class="dcard-t">What time zone does Aion 2 use?</span><span class="dcard-c">+</span><span class="dcard-body hidden">The Taiwan service runs on UTC+8 (Asia/Taipei) and the Korea service on UTC+9 (Asia/Seoul). Both use the same clock schedule, so every event happens one hour apart between them. Global NA, SA, EU and Japan servers open October 5, 2026 and their server clock has not been published yet.</span></button><button class="dcard" type="button" data-label="FAQ"><span class="dcard-t">Why is my Aion 2 rift timer an hour off?</span><span class="dcard-c">+</span><span class="dcard-body hidden">Most often you have the wrong server selected, since Korea and Taiwan run one hour apart. Some trackers also hard-code US Eastern hours, which drift by an hour whenever daylight saving changes. This page anchors every event to the server&#x27;s IANA time zone, so it stays correct through DST.</span></button><button class="dcard" type="button" data-label="FAQ"><span class="dcard-t">What time is the daily and weekly reset in Aion 2?</span><span class="dcard-c">+</span><span class="dcard-body hidden">Daily reset is at 05:00 server time. Weekly reset is Wednesday at 05:00 server time. Daily dungeon entries (7 per week) do not require daily logins and can all be cleared before Wednesday.</span></button><button class="dcard" type="button" data-label="FAQ"><span class="dcard-t">When do Aion 2 world bosses spawn?</span><span class="dcard-c">+</span><span class="dcard-body hidden">Post-Conquest Reshanta bosses (Watcher Kaira, Executor Argo, Executor Kaira, Executor Tamasa, Executioner Dramos, Ravager Marakha, Turncoat Ducal) spawn Wednesday and Saturday at 22:30 server time and despawn 30 minutes later. Enraged Guardian Lord Nahma spawns Friday and Sunday at 22:00. Watcher Kaira also has a regular 4-hour cycle from 01:00.</span></button><button class="dcard" type="button" data-label="FAQ"><span class="dcard-t">When is Spacetime Rift Domination and the Abyss Rift Zone?</span><span class="dcard-c">+</span><span class="dcard-body hidden">Rift Domination runs Monday, Thursday and Saturday at 20:00 and 23:00 server time with a 5-minute prep and a 15-minute match. The Abyss Rift Zone battlefield queues Tuesday and Thursday at 22:00 server time. Artifact Conquest is Wednesday and Saturday at 22:00.</span></button><button class="dcard" type="button" data-label="FAQ"><span class="dcard-t">When is the Aion 2 global release?</span><span class="dcard-c">+</span><span class="dcard-body hidden">Aion 2 launches globally on Monday, October 5, 2026 at 6:00 AM PDT (13:00 UTC) on Steam and the PURPLE launcher, with servers for North America, South America, Europe and Japan. Founder&#x27;s Pack Advance Access runs from September 30 to October 4 and opened September 30 at 7:00 AM PDT (14:00 UTC), one hour later than first planned. This page counts down to both in your local time.</span></button><button class="dcard" type="button" data-label="FAQ"><span class="dcard-t">Can I get Aion 2 rift alerts in Discord or on stream?</span><span class="dcard-c">+</span><span class="dcard-body hidden">Yes. Paste a Discord webhook URL into the Discord alerts section and our server posts a message before each event you enable, even when this page is closed. The streamer section builds an OBS browser-source overlay URL with a live rift countdown, ticker bar, next-up cards or checklist.</span></button><button class="dcard" type="button" data-label="FAQ"><span class="dcard-t">How many classes are in Aion 2?</span><span class="dcard-c">+</span><span class="dcard-body hidden">Aion 2 has 9 playable classes: Gladiator, Templar, Assassin, Ranger, Sorcerer, Spiritmaster, Cleric, Chanter and Brawler. Every class is available to both factions and can be played male or female, so your class choice never locks you out of a side.</span></button><button class="dcard" type="button" data-label="FAQ"><span class="dcard-t">What is on the Aion 2 schedule today?</span><span class="dcard-c">+</span><span class="dcard-body hidden">Spacetime Rifts run every 3 hours at 02:00, 05:00, 08:00, 11:00, 14:00, 17:00, 20:00 and 23:00 server time, the daily reset lands at 05:00 server time and the weekly reset on Wednesday at 05:00. World bosses, Shugo Festival, Dimensional Invasion and Beritra Air Raid sit on their own rotations, and the schedule on this page converts all of them into your own time zone.</span></button></div></section>
<!-- Info -->
<section class="section only-full" id="info">
  <div class="section-head"><div><div class="eyebrow">Know before you go</div><h2>Quick reference</h2></div></div>
  <div class="grid cols-2" id="infoGrid"></div>
</section>

</main>
